00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:05.691
right now, still illegal,
but they made it legal

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.994
to essentially go harvest
ballots in California.

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.529
So I think a combination

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:14.534
of basically the whole
state awash in ballots,

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Democratic Party
awash with money

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.672
so that they can afford
to pay as many people

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:22.275
as they need to go
pick up ballots.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.509
It's made it very hard.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:24.777
You can only kind of
go to those places

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.479
that are almost like the Alamo.

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:28.047
You have to actually have money.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:30.383
If you get targeted, like
I have been several times

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.418
for the last few
election cycles,

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.554 align:start size:81% position:19%
we had to actually
go raise money

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:37.356
from all over the nation
so we could fight back.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.659 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I think that's
gonna be the one place,

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.561
you say, is there any hope?

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:45.364 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, there's 52
congressional districts there.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.033
They gerrymandered
the hell out of it

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:49.402 align:start size:84% position:16%
with this commission
this last time.

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:52.205
But I actually think
that it is possible

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:54.674 align:start size:81% position:19%
that we could pick
up two or three

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:57.276
or four congressional
seats in California.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.645 align:start position:0%
And look, that has not been
possible for the last 10 years.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.648 align:start size:97% position:3%
So that's probably the
only bright side right now.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:05.084
Obviously, you had the crazy DA

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:07.253
that got beat in San Francisco.

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
There may be a recall from
the one in Los Angeles.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.092
But look, I'll just tell you,

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.962
I was in Sarasota
for a couple weeks,

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.630
and kind of the first time

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we got the
headquarters going,

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.834 align:start size:81% position:19%
and then went back
to California,

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:24.103
had not been back
for a couple weeks.

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:27.573
And I was greeted at
the little donut shop

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:30.843
that I go to get a cup of
coffee by a homeless guy,

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:33.579
like standing in front
there, with his bike,

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.182
essentially not letting you
in until you give him money.

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
The owner of the business
can't do anything.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, you know this
'cause you just left there.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.955
But I just don't know.

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:44.724
I think people get a little bit,

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:46.893
it's almost like
Stockholm Syndrome,

00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:49.328 align:start size:88% position:13%
and people have just
become accustomed to it.

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:52.932 align:start position:0%
What started, probably, I
remember five or six years ago,

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:57.370
there was a church in my home
city, Tulare-Visalia area,

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.705
65,000 people in Tulare.

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:03.409 align:start position:0%
And there's a church that
said, oh, well, we're a church.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.144
We're gonna help people.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:06.579
Good thing. They
wanna help people.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.981 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, there was a couple
homeless people living there.

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:12.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, pretty soon it went
from two to 10 to 24,

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:14.053 align:start size:88% position:13%
to when the church
said, whoa, whoa, whoa,

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.455
we can't have this in
our church parking lot.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.424
Well, now there's just
homeless scattered out

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:19.892
through the whole city.

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:23.329
I mean, there's hundreds and
hundreds, just in my home city.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:25.264
And that doesn't include the
district that I represented.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.632
There was homeless
everywhere there.

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:28.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
And of course, you
know what it is in LA.

00:09:28.668 --> 00:09:32.672
But I think that's just
spending all this time

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:37.476
in California and Washington
DC, the last decade or so,

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.478
when you come to a
state like Florida,

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:41.614 align:start size:84% position:16%
you realize like,
whoa, wait a second.

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:43.816 align:start size:84% position:16%
I just had a flashback
to what it was like

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:46.385 align:start size:88% position:13%
