00:29:35.673 --> 00:29:37.108
you could go on Social Blade,

00:29:37.108 --> 00:29:39.077
where they did a live
track of subscribers.

00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:40.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you could literally
just watch a graph

00:29:40.779 --> 00:29:42.280
and the numbers would grow.

00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:46.751
And every time I got within
about 20,000 of a million,

00:29:46.751 --> 00:29:49.554
I would lose 50,000, and then
it would slowly grow again.

00:29:49.554 --> 00:29:51.289
And then I'd lose 40,000.

00:29:51.289 --> 00:29:54.492
And it took me months when it
should have been way before.

00:29:54.492 --> 00:29:55.960
And then what did
Social Blade do?

00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:59.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, YouTube
deactivated their API

00:29:59.130 --> 00:30:01.032 align:start size:88% position:13%
so they could no longer
track in real time

00:30:01.032 --> 00:30:02.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it was
becoming too obvious.

00:30:02.834 --> 00:30:04.202
So one of the things that I say

00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:06.237 line:0%
all the time about social media,

00:30:06.237 --> 00:30:08.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
it's not the stuff that
we know that they're doing

00:30:08.506 --> 00:30:11.543 line:0%
I'm worried about, it's the
stuff that we do not know

00:30:11.543 --> 00:30:13.144
that I'm most worried about.

00:30:13.144 --> 00:30:14.112
So, okay.

00:30:14.112 --> 00:30:16.581
So all of that added up.

00:30:16.581 --> 00:30:20.051 align:start size:97% position:3%
How is Truth going to
solve some of the problems?

00:30:20.051 --> 00:30:21.953
We could go into all
of the shadow banning.

00:30:21.953 --> 00:30:23.922
You don't see subscriber videos,

00:30:24.956 --> 00:30:26.558 align:start size:88% position:13%
the bans, the
censorship, okay, fine.

00:30:26.558 --> 00:30:27.392
We can do all that.

00:30:27.392 --> 00:30:28.593
My audience gets it.

00:30:28.593 --> 00:30:30.895 align:start size:88% position:13%
How is Truth gonna solve
some of this stuff?

00:30:30.895 --> 00:30:33.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, so look, one of
the things that we're doing

00:30:33.298 --> 00:30:34.499
is we're riding on top of,

00:30:34.499 --> 00:30:37.101 align:start size:88% position:13%
we call it riding on
the Rumble rails, right?

00:30:37.101 --> 00:30:39.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the same thing
that Locals is using,

00:30:39.237 --> 00:30:41.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
Rumble is getting
into that marketplace.

00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:42.307
It's critically important

00:30:42.307 --> 00:30:45.143
because we have to
have data centers

00:30:45.143 --> 00:30:49.280 align:start size:84% position:16%
that these big giant
tech companies can't
kill and cut off.

00:30:49.280 --> 00:30:52.884 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's why we've
partnered with Rumble,

00:30:52.884 --> 00:30:54.185
and then what we're doing,

00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:57.689
the product that we're
building out right now

00:30:57.689 --> 00:31:01.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
is one that we envision
is taking kind of the best

00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:04.796
of all of these social media
companies that are out there,

00:31:06.231 --> 00:31:09.133
in terms of, Twitter's kind of
just a simple message board,

00:31:09.133 --> 00:31:10.702
then you have a lot
better technology

00:31:10.702 --> 00:31:13.671 align:start size:84% position:16%
at Instagram,
Facebook, and TikTok.

00:31:13.671 --> 00:31:16.307
So we're trying to take
the best of all of that

00:31:16.307 --> 00:31:18.009
and put it into one platform,

00:31:18.009 --> 00:31:21.546
and people who have
seen Truth Social,

00:31:22.981 --> 00:31:25.817
which we're only just a
few months old right now.

00:31:25.817 --> 00:31:29.487
And right now, we just have
a simple chronological feed.

00:31:29.487 --> 00:31:30.922
No, we don't use any algorithms,

00:31:30.922 --> 00:31:32.991 align:start size:88% position:13%
but you will see already
that we are trying

00:31:32.991 --> 00:31:35.660 align:start size:84% position:16%
to do a really good
job with video,

00:31:35.660 --> 00:31:37.929
and no surprise,
we're using Rumble

00:31:37.929 --> 00:31:40.265
for our video infrastructure.

00:31:40.265 --> 00:31:43.034
So we're trying to tie
all of this together

00:31:43.034 --> 00:31:45.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that we have a product
that takes the best

00:31:45.036 --> 00:31:46.537
of all these social
media companies,

00:31:46.537 --> 00:31:49.073
because, and I said that
we would come back to this,

00:31:49.073 --> 00:31:53.711 align:start size:88% position:13%
and here we are, the
eyeballs in this country

00:31:53.711 --> 00:31:57.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
are on Instagram and
at TikTok, right?

00:31:57.882 --> 00:32:00.618
You essentially have kind
of an older demographic

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:03.521
that are on Facebook that are
probably over the age of 50.

00:32:03.521 --> 00:32:07.392
From 50 down to 25, Instagram
just dominates the market.

00:32:07.392 --> 00:32:09.227
And then under 25,

00:32:09.227 --> 00:32:13.431
which just is really scary as
hell, Chinese-owned TikTok,

00:32:13.431 --> 00:32:15.800
and all these young
people on TikTok.

00:32:18.469 --> 00:32:20.071
For us to compete with Twitter,

00:32:20.071 --> 00:32:23.408 align:start size:84% position:16%
like, look, we're
not gonna ban people.

00:32:23.408 --> 00:32:25.009
That's kind of an
easy market for us.

00:32:25.009 --> 00:32:26.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like people that
wanna be on Twitter,

00:32:26.244 --> 00:32:27.745
get news, that sort of thing,

00:32:27.745 --> 00:32:29.414
'cause Twitter sucks so bad.

00:32:29.414 --> 00:32:33.184 align:start position:0%
And a lot of our people are
never gonna go back to Twitter.

00:32:33.184 --> 00:32:35.987
So that's kind of
an easy market.

00:32:35.987 --> 00:32:37.822
But to really grow this company,

00:32:37.822 --> 00:32:41.426 align:start size:88% position:13%
we've gotta get into
the mainstream of people

00:32:41.426 --> 00:32:44.762 align:start position:0%
that don't wanna just do
politics and news all the time,

00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:48.366
but wanna communicate and
actually social network,

00:32:49.801 --> 00:32:52.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing that we're not
gonna shove some algorithm

00:32:52.003 --> 00:32:54.272
in their face, I think that's
our comparative advantage,

00:32:54.272 --> 00:32:58.576
is we're gonna do a lot
of things really well,

00:32:58.576 --> 00:33:00.011 align:start size:81% position:19%
but you're not
gonna be canceled.

00:33:00.011 --> 00:33:01.546
We're not gonna steal your data.

00:33:01.546 --> 00:33:03.181
We're not gonna shove some
algorithm into your phone

00:33:03.181 --> 00:33:05.316
on the stuff that we
think you need to see.

00:33:05.316 --> 00:33:06.918 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's our
comparative advantage.

00:33:06.918 --> 00:33:08.853
And it's really just about
filling out the feature set.

00:33:08.853 --> 00:33:11.289
So we're in the Apple App Store.

00:33:11.289 --> 00:33:12.590
We've been there for
a couple months now.

00:33:12.590 --> 00:33:14.759
We just got truthsocial.com.

00:33:14.759 --> 00:33:17.895
Now anybody can sign
up from any device,

00:33:17.895 --> 00:33:19.530
including you can
sign up on Android,

00:33:19.530 --> 00:33:21.966
but you just have to kind
of bookmark it and go back.

00:33:21.966 --> 00:33:23.234
And then we're hopeful

00:33:23.234 --> 00:33:26.337
to get into the Google
Play Store here soon,

00:33:26.337 --> 00:33:29.474 align:start size:97% position:3%
so then it's simple for
people that like to have apps,

00:33:29.474 --> 00:33:31.809
and then it's really
about the features

00:33:31.809 --> 00:33:33.478
that we're gonna be rolling out.

00:33:33.478 --> 00:33:36.714
- So the features,
people love features.

00:33:36.714 --> 00:33:38.116
There'll be more
features for sure.

00:33:38.116 --> 00:33:40.284
But how worried are
you about just some

00:33:40.284 --> 00:33:42.720 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the way the
internet works now?

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:45.823
So for example, Truth
is in the App Store.

00:33:47.125 --> 00:33:48.826
Twitter booted Trump,

00:33:48.826 --> 00:33:52.830
and then there was this
concern that if Elon,

00:33:52.830 --> 00:33:56.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
if he ends up getting Twitter,
and he puts Trump back on,

00:33:56.667 --> 00:33:58.169
if Trump was to go back on,

00:33:58.169 --> 00:33:59.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though Trump has
said he won't go back on,

00:33:59.203 --> 00:34:00.838
he's all-in on Truth,

00:34:00.838 --> 00:34:02.707 align:start size:88% position:13%
but the App Store could
then boot Twitter.

00:34:02.707 --> 00:34:05.977
That this is multi-layered
at many different levels.

00:34:05.977 --> 00:34:08.479
- Yeah, so you cut right to it.

00:34:10.481 --> 00:34:14.852
The reason that we
went to Apple first,

00:34:16.287 --> 00:34:19.690
I've had a long, my whole
career, I dealt with Apple.

00:34:21.292 --> 00:34:25.263
They're less woke than others.

00:34:25.263 --> 00:34:27.131 align:start size:88% position:13%
They do have Republicans
that work there.

00:34:27.131 --> 00:34:28.633
I dealt with 'em
