00:36:05.129 --> 00:36:06.898
So I think they are
a little bit worried

00:36:06.898 --> 00:36:09.967
about what Republicans
could ultimately do.

00:36:09.967 --> 00:36:12.270 align:start size:84% position:16%
So look, I think
here at Truth Social,

00:36:12.270 --> 00:36:14.272
we're a family friendly place.

00:36:14.272 --> 00:36:16.541 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're just not gonna
censor people for politics.

00:36:16.541 --> 00:36:17.708 align:start size:81% position:19%
You can talk about
any damn thing

00:36:17.708 --> 00:36:19.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
you want on the
platform politically,

00:36:21.145 --> 00:36:22.547
but we don't want a
lot of the garbage

00:36:22.547 --> 00:36:24.916
that I think they would
try to use to wedge,

00:36:24.916 --> 00:36:26.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
to get us kicked
off these platforms,

00:36:26.751 --> 00:36:29.253
and that's to our advantage.

00:36:29.253 --> 00:36:32.523 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So when Elon, now it's
about two months ago,

00:36:32.523 --> 00:36:35.693 align:start size:97% position:3%
first started grumbling
about maybe buying Twitter,

00:36:35.693 --> 00:36:37.562
how were you feeling about it?

00:36:37.562 --> 00:36:40.298
And how did you feel
when President Trump...

00:36:40.298 --> 00:36:42.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, I don't remember
which order it was.

00:36:42.233 --> 00:36:44.602
Did President Trump first
say he wasn't gonna do it,

00:36:44.602 --> 00:36:46.604 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then sort of went
after Elon a little bit,

00:36:46.604 --> 00:36:48.072
or was it the other way around,

00:36:48.072 --> 00:36:50.408
and what do you make of him
just getting in the mix?

00:36:50.408 --> 00:36:52.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I don't
make much of the...

00:36:52.777 --> 00:36:54.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've only met
Elon Musk a couple times,

00:36:54.912 --> 00:36:57.248 align:start size:97% position:3%
but he seems like he's real,
obviously brilliant guy.

00:36:57.248 --> 00:36:59.717
Very, very sharp, but kind
of very funny guy, right?

00:36:59.717 --> 00:37:03.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's why he has a big
following on social media

00:37:03.955 --> 00:37:08.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's a creative
dude, but if you remember,

00:37:08.526 --> 00:37:10.494
and the fake news has
basically ignored this,

00:37:10.494 --> 00:37:14.765 align:start size:97% position:3%
surprise, surprise, but
the mission of our company,

00:37:14.765 --> 00:37:16.667
Truth Social, is very simple.

00:37:16.667 --> 00:37:20.571
Like we're here to open
the internet back up

00:37:20.571 --> 00:37:23.040 align:start size:81% position:19%
and give people
their voices back.

00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:26.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very simple
business plan and mission.

00:37:26.644 --> 00:37:30.114
And so I like to say
that President Trump

00:37:30.114 --> 00:37:31.782
didn't need a new business,

00:37:31.782 --> 00:37:34.552 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I sure as hell
didn't need a new job.

00:37:34.552 --> 00:37:37.188
It's just that, what the
hell do you expect us to do

00:37:37.188 --> 00:37:39.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you kick all these
people off of social media?

00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:41.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
Including the former
president of United States,

00:37:41.192 --> 00:37:42.960
who had no voice at all,

00:37:42.960 --> 00:37:46.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
plus millions of his
followers had no voice at all,

00:37:46.764 --> 00:37:50.034 align:start position:0%
not to mention all the censoring
that we already discussed.

00:37:51.235 --> 00:37:53.271
So the fake news
has ignored this,

00:37:53.271 --> 00:37:55.239
but when it came out originally

00:37:55.239 --> 00:37:57.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Elon Musk was
looking at buying Twitter,

00:37:57.608 --> 00:37:58.976
we're like, hey, go for it.

00:37:58.976 --> 00:38:00.511
Like that's our mission.

00:38:00.511 --> 00:38:03.080
Like if you can bust up one
of those big tech companies,

00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:04.949
great, have at it.

00:38:04.949 --> 00:38:07.585 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so we've always
been supportive of it.

00:38:07.585 --> 00:38:08.786
But at the same time,

00:38:08.786 --> 00:38:10.288
what I said from
the very beginning,

00:38:10.288 --> 00:38:12.757 align:start size:88% position:13%
I said, look, the place
needs a lot of work

00:38:12.757 --> 00:38:15.159
because there's a hell
of a lot of bots there.

00:38:15.159 --> 00:38:16.827
And we already knew that.

00:38:16.827 --> 00:38:20.765 align:start size:97% position:3%
I knew that from my experience
on having a Parlor account,

00:38:20.765 --> 00:38:24.035
a Rumble account, having
a big Twitter account,

00:38:24.035 --> 00:38:27.638
And then also just in our beta
test period on Truth Social,

00:38:27.638 --> 00:38:29.874
how is that possible that people

00:38:29.874 --> 00:38:32.276
who had been on Twitter forever,

00:38:32.276 --> 00:38:34.779
and Instagram, in many cases,

00:38:34.779 --> 00:38:37.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
most people were
getting more engagement

00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:40.318 align:start size:84% position:16%
on our platform
during beta testing

00:38:40.318 --> 00:38:42.286
than they were getting on
these big tech platforms.

00:38:42.286 --> 00:38:44.255
Now you can say some of
that's shadow banning,

00:38:44.255 --> 00:38:45.489
some of that's censoring,

00:38:45.489 --> 00:38:48.592
but I think it's
also that Twitter,

00:38:48.592 --> 00:38:49.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you notice I've spent
a lot of time talking

00:38:49.994 --> 00:38:51.529 align:start size:84% position:16%
about Facebook,
Instagram, and TikTok.

00:38:51.529 --> 00:38:52.496
There's a reason.

00:38:53.664 --> 00:38:56.400
Twitter is just
a global PR wire.

00:38:56.400 --> 00:38:58.669
It's where when Barack Obama
wants to make a statement,

00:38:58.669 --> 00:38:59.904
like he did last week.

00:38:59.904 --> 00:39:02.073
He hadn't been on
Twitter forever.

00:39:02.073 --> 00:39:03.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I dunno, he
made some statement,

00:39:03.341 --> 00:39:05.876
I think, about the
shooting in Texas.

00:39:05.876 --> 00:39:08.713 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, it's a place
for celebrities

00:39:08.713 --> 00:39:12.350 align:start size:97% position:3%
and political hacks and
reporters to go put stuff out.

00:39:12.350 --> 00:39:16.053
It's not where people
go to social network.

00:39:16.053 --> 00:39:18.756
So from my perspective,

00:39:20.224 --> 00:39:22.093
we're all for opening
this thing back up.

00:39:22.093 --> 00:39:25.229 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's a global platform,
meaning Twitter.

00:39:25.229 --> 00:39:26.464 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know if
Elon's gonna do it,

00:39:26.464 --> 00:39:27.998
but I think what
he's realized now

00:39:27.998 --> 00:39:32.570
is what we knew going back
is that it's full of bots,

00:39:33.771 --> 00:39:36.040
and bot is a kind of a big term,

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:38.242
but it's basically, it's
a combination of bots,

00:39:38.242 --> 00:39:41.946 align:start size:97% position:3%
spam accounts, fake
